$COMMAND SUMMARY - S IS SIGN - N IS NUMBER [TYPE # FOR MAX]
  SN TO MOVE RIGHT [S=+] OR LEFT [S=-] N LINES AND TYPE LINE
  NA TO APPEND N LINES
  SB TO MOVE TO BEGINNING [S=+] OR END [S=-]
  SNC TO MOVE N CHARACTERS RIGHT OR LEFT$
  SND TO DELETE N CHARACTERS RIGHT OR LEFT
  E TO EXIT
  NFSTRING TO FIND NTH OCCURENCE OF STRING
  H TO RETURN TO HEAD OF FILE
  I TO INSERT TEXT
  SNK TO KILL N LINES RIGHT OR LEFT
  SNL TO MOVE N LINES RIGHT OR LEFT$
  NM TO DO MACRO N TIMES
  O TO RESTART WITH ORIGINAL FILE
  Q TO QUIT WITHOUT ALTERING FILE
  RNAME TO READ LIBRARY FILE
  NSSTRING1[CTL-Z]STRING2 TO SUBSTITUTE STRING2 FOR STRING1
  SNT TO TYPE N LINES RIGHT OR LEFT$
